# Used ONLY by Prisma migrations, from your own machine. Never bundled into the
# app — the browser uses the anon key in .env.local instead.
#
# Get it from: Supabase dashboard -> Connect -> ORMs -> Prisma
#
# TWO THINGS THE DASHBOARD WILL GET WRONG FOR THIS PROJECT:
#
#   1. It pastes a literal [YOUR-PASSWORD] placeholder. Replace it with the
#      real password (the one in Secret.txt). If the password contains any of
#      : / ? # [ ] @ then URL-encode those characters.
#
#   2. It defaults to port 6543, the TRANSACTION pooler. Migrations need a
#      session-level connection — use port 5432.
#
# Note: Prisma 7 removed `directUrl`. Only DATABASE_URL is read (see
# prisma.config.ts), so it must be the 5432 one.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.YOUR-PROJECT-REF:YOUR-REAL-PASSWORD@aws-0-YOUR-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"
